// COMMITTED third-party fixtures — per-image-kind rasters the image
// reducer batteries need. dart-pdf cannot write Gray, CMYK, Indexed or
// 1-bit CCITT images, so these were produced ONCE by ImageMagick and the
// bytes are committed (a few KB each in git; excluded from the pub
// archive by .pubignore).
//
// Provenance (macOS, 2026-09-12):
//   ImageMagick 7.1.2-25 Q16-HDRI aarch64 037e46295:20260604 https://imagemagick.org
//   Source raster: the generator's 128² photo raster, `buildPhotoPng()`,
//   resized to 64².
//
//   magick photo.png -resize 64x64! -colorspace Gray -depth 8 -density 288 -units PixelsPerInch -compress Zip     gray.pdf
//   magick photo.png -resize 64x64! -colorspace CMYK -depth 8 -density 288 -units PixelsPerInch -compress JPEG    cmyk_jpeg.pdf
//   magick photo.png -resize 64x64! -type Palette -colors 16 -depth 8 -density 288 -units PixelsPerInch -compress Zip indexed.pdf
//   magick photo.png -resize 64x64! -monochrome -density 1200 -units PixelsPerInch -compress Group4                 bilevel_g4.pdf
//
// `indexed.pdf` was asked for 4-bit indices; this ImageMagick build
// always writes an 8-bit index for the PDF Palette coder (verified with
// `pdfimages -list`), so `bits: 8` is declared per the brief's own
// documented fallback. Two further shapes (a Flate-stored, non-CCITT
// 1-bit gray image, and a 16-bit-per-component image) were attempted
// with ImageMagick and with Pillow 12.2 and neither tool can write
// them into a PDF at all — those two kinds are hand-authored instead,
// as `bilevelRawPdf` and `gray16RawPdf` in `handwritten.dart`.

